# Foundry already writes zip snapshots here. Do not git them.
Backups/
# Daily debug/error logs. Huge, rotated, not campaign data.
Logs/
# LevelDB lock + text journals. Rewritten every time Foundry starts.
# Harmless at runtime, noisy in git.
**/LOCK
**/LOG
**/LOG.old
# Numbered LevelDB write-ahead logs (e.g. data/scenes/000758.log).
# After compaction they are often empty and byte-identical across packs,
# so git treats them as "renames" between worlds/modules. A merge that
# applies those renames will mix databases.
*.log
# Modules and systems are reinstallable from Foundry's package installer.
# Their compendium databases churn on every world launch and dominated
# the diffs without containing Pass the Torch content.
Data/modules/
Data/systems/
# OS junk
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
